{
  "_why": "Dotted paths (list indexes as numbers) that may differ from a broker ledger golden, keyed <lane>/<golden> (e.g. demand/transitions); aged.json is an input, held to the merge-base's copy. Each entry names one exact path; a wildcard is refused. Empty: no difference is allowed. A PR that changes a ledger's behaviour on purpose names each path it changes here; the edit is reviewed with the PR, and the integrity job (bin/goldens/golden-integrity.py) holds the committed goldens to the merge-base tree's behaviour everywhere else, fails on an entry that explains no difference or that the merge-base already carried, and on the push to main fails until a merged change's entries are cleared. This change (2026-11-19, medchron_progress): the medchron_jobs table gains the nullable kind, stage and expected_finish columns by an additive, idempotent migration, so every medchron schema, row and table dump gains those three; the projection (and so every status, list and record reply) gains kind and stage; the status reads gain clients; and the new read-only medchron_update_files verb answers in the verbs golden.",
